{"type":"message","id":"58b0706d","parentId":"5652fd1d","timestamp":"2026-05-26T07:15:35.600Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST /send endpoint returns error code 1101 regardless of auth method. This is a CF Workers error indicating the request was aborted (ERROR_CODE_CONTENT_DRIFT_DETECTED) or similar. However the GET /history endpoint works fine with the same auth header.\n\nIt seems the send endpoint has an issue. Let me check if there's a different endpoint format expected, or if the API just has a bug with the send endpoint.\n\nSince I can read the history (proving auth works) but can't send messages (error 1101), this appears to be a platform issue, not an auth issue.\n\nThe heartbeat check is otherwise complete: both threads show no human messages, just automated heartbeat posts from the system. The gap from 23:50 UTC to 07:15 UTC (445 minutes) is noted.\n","thinkingSignature":"380101d582b9ea099dcd829bf6c966c612311973e70f68e805447cf0dca1af72"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**ECHO Platform Heartbeat Check - 07:15 UTC | 2026-05-26**\n\n| Thread | Status | Last Record | Gap |\n|--------|--------|-------------|-----|\n| `arbitration` | ✅ Auth OK | 23:50 UTC (05-25) | ~445 min |\n| `general` | ✅ Auth OK | 23:50 UTC (05-25) | ~445 min |\n\n**Findings:**\n- ✅ GET /history works with `X-API-Key` header\n- ⚠️ POST /send returns error 1101 (CF Workers abort error - platform issue, not auth)\n- Both threads: **No human messages** — all posts are automated heartbeats\n- **断档确认**: 445-minute gap detected (23:50 UTC → 07:15 UTC)\n\nPlatform is accessible for reading but the send endpoint has an issue preventing heartbeat posts from being delivered. This may need platform-level investigation."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":169,"output":363,"cacheRead":20736,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21268,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"sto